From: tompta1 <546706+tompta1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:39:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: pinctrl: describe the T8011 S8000-compatible
 GPIO block

T8011 uses the existing S8000 pin-function semantics. Describe the explicit chip compatible and its two fallbacks.

[Orchard: from OrchardLinux/orchard#205 (tompta1, 09038adf),
 kernel/patches/drivers/pinctrl/0004-dt-bindings-pinctrl-describe-the-T8011-S8000-compati.patch; rebased onto main, otherwise unchanged.]

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pinctrl/apple,pinctrl.yaml | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pinctrl/apple,pinctrl.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pinctrl/apple,pinctrl.yaml
index f08d2c4f5..0fb1d8cb0 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pinctrl/apple,pinctrl.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pinctrl/apple,pinctrl.yaml
@@ -17,6 +17,10 @@ description: |
 properties:
   compatible:
     oneOf:
+      - items:
+          - const: apple,t8011-pinctrl
+          - const: apple,s8000-pinctrl
+          - const: apple,pinctrl
       - items:
           - enum:
               - apple,t6020-pinctrl
